# E2E Testing Rules

## Always Run With HTML Report

ALWAYS add `--reporter=html` when running E2E tests so the report can be shared:

```bash
npx playwright test --reporter=html
```

## Parallelism & Timeout

- Default: **40 workers** (`--workers=40`)
- First round of any new E2E run: **15s timeout** (`--timeout=15000`)
- Subsequent rounds if failures remain: increase timeout incrementally (30s, 60s)
- Run multiple rounds until **all tests pass**

```bash
# Standard command
npx playwright test --reporter=html --workers=40 --timeout=15000

# With specific file
npx playwright test e2e/some.spec.ts --reporter=html --workers=40 --timeout=15000
```

## Fix ALL Errors — No Ignoring

- If any error is found during testing (including pre-existing, unrelated, or not directly touched), **fix it immediately** before moving on.
- Never skip, suppress, or defer errors. Own the entire codebase quality.
- After fixing, re-run affected tests to confirm the fix.

## Monolithic File Threshold

A file is considered **monolithic** when it has **≥ 900 lines**. When found:
1. Split into focused modules/hooks/utils
2. Remove redundant code
3. Ensure unit tests cover all extracted modules at > 90%
4. Add E2E tests for any new user-facing behaviour
